    "created_at": "2024-03-01T12:46:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-01T12:46:55Z",
    "body": "I think one example why you wouldn't want to enforce a DNS limit on URLs is something like Tor onion URLs.\r\nAs far as I can tell right now it's `http://[56characters].onion` - but since Tor doesn't use DNS to resolve this address, it shouldn't necessarily be limited by it.",
